{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"d8b978f1-3247-413e-928d-a11b7f73ac0a","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The 500 error occurs because the `similar` list stored in DynamoDB contains **float** values (the raw result of `similarity`). DynamoDB does not accept native Python floats, which raises `TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.` on the second publish attempt.\n\n**Fix applied**\n- Updated `related()` in `src/app.py` to convert each score to a `Decimal` (`Decimal(str(score))`) before storing.\n- Added a detailed docstring explaining the conversion and its necessity.\n- Imported `Decimal` locally within the function to avoid unnecessary global imports.\n\nThis prevents the `TypeError` and ensures subsequent publications succeed.\n\nYou can review the full explanation and the implemented changes in the generated report:\n\n[ANSWER.md](/Users/valentinakoniukhova/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/d8b978f1-3247-413e-928d-a11b7f73ac0a/ANSWER.md)\n","duration_seconds":34.90756,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":11689,"output_tokens":2500,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":73600,"total_tokens":14189}}}
